# Compile targets for Next.js 15.5.
#
# Do not replace this with `baseline widely available`.
# Next 15.5.24's compiled browserslist rejects that query. getSupportedBrowsers()
# swallows the error and falls back to Chrome 64 / Safari 12, which is the
# target that keeps the legacy polyfills in the client runtime.
# browserslist 4.29.5 (November 2026) resolves the query to Chrome 124+,
# Firefox 126+, and Safari / iOS Safari 17.5+. That drops iOS Safari 16.
#
# This is the explicit modern floor that still includes iOS Safari 16:
# Chrome, Edge, and Firefox 111, Safari and iOS Safari 16, Opera 97
# (Chromium 111). Every API the legacy-JavaScript audit flags is already
# native there (Safari 15.4 / Chrome 93). Lines are combined with OR.
# Do not add a bare `defaults` or `not dead` line.

chrome >= 111
edge >= 111
firefox >= 111
safari >= 16
ios_saf >= 16
opera >= 97
